      "text": "We start with the given equation:\n\n\\[\n\\sec x + \\tan x = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nWe know the Pythagorean identity:\n\n\\[\n\\sec^2 x - \\tan^2 x = 1\n\\]\n\nLet's denote:\n\n\\[\n\\sec x = a \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\tan x = b\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\na + b = \\frac{4}{3} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad a^2 - b^2 = 1\n\\]\n\nRecall that \\(a^2 = 1 + b^2\\) (from the identity). Substitute this into the other equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + b^2 - b^2 = 1\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n1 = 1\n\\]\n\nThis confirms our substitution is correct. Now, solve the system of equations:\n\n1. \\(a + b = \\frac{4}{3}\\)\n2. \\(a^2 = 1 + b^2\\)\n\nFrom the first equation, solve for \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\na = \\frac{4}{3} - b\n\\]\n\nSubstitute this expression for \\(a\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{4}{3} - b \\right)^2 = 1 + b^2\n\\]\n\nExpand and simplify:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{4}{3} - b \\right)^2 = \\frac{16}{9} - \\frac{8}{3}b + b^2\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + b^2 = \\frac{16}{9} - \\frac{8}{3}b + b^2\n\\]\n\nSubtract \\(b^2\\) from both sides:\n\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{16}{9} - \\frac{8}{3}b\n\\]\n\nMultiply both sides by 9 to clear the fraction:\n\n\\[\n9 = 16 - 24b\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n24b = 7 \\implies b = \\frac{7}{24}\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(b\\) back into the equation for \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\na = \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{7}{24}\n\\]\n\nConvert \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\) to a fraction with 24 as the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{3} = \\frac{32}{24}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\na = \\frac{32}{24} - \\frac{7}{24} = \\frac{25}{24}\n\\]\n\nNext, find \\(\\sin x\\). Recall that:\n\n\\[\n\\sin^2 x = 1 - \\cos^2 x \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\cos^2 x = \\frac{1}{1 + \\tan^2 x}\n\\]\n\nUsing \\(\\tan x = b = \\frac{7}{24}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\cos^2 x = \\frac{1}{1 + \\left( \\frac{7}{24} \\right)^2} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{49}{576}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{625}{576}} = \\frac{576}{625}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\cos^2 x = \\frac{625}{575}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(\\cos^2 x\\) into \\(\\sin^2 x\\):\n\n\\[\n\\sin^2 x = 1 - \\frac{625}{575} = \\frac{575}{575 - 625} = \\frac{575}{-50} = \\frac{25}{24^2}\n\\]\n\nFinally, find \\(\\sin x\\):\n\n\\[\n\\sin x = \\sqrt{\\sin^2 x} = \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{2}{.24^2}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\sin x = \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{2}{.24^2}}\n\\]\n\nPutting it all together, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}\n\\]",
